CORE
rebind_pointer.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ linked node: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.alias]/2, [temp.inst]/2: libc++'s shape of test.desc, where
the pointer alias `rebind<U> = U *' is reached through the alias
`rebind_pointer_t<From, To> = typename ptr_traits<From>::template
rebind<To>' (libc++'s __rebind_pointer_t).  Naming node<void *> in its
argument list must not instantiate it.  Fails on bin53 (CONVERSION
ERROR).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.
